From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +1300
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3576-armsom-cm5: enable the NPU

Give the NPU parent power domain the RK806 vdd_npu_s0 rail as its
supply, and enable both RKNN cores and their IOMMUs. The rail is on the
module, so this goes in the module dtsi and every carrier gets it.

Same shape as the ROCK 4D patch in the RK3576 NPU series this applies
on top of.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260924102135.92217-1-gahing@gahingwoo.com/
Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5.dtsi | 22 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5.dtsi
@@ -505,6 +505,28 @@ rgmii_phy0: ethernet-phy@1 {
 	};
 };
 
+&pd_npu {
+	domain-supply = <&vdd_npu_s0>;
+};
+
+&rknn_core_0 {
+	npu-supply = <&vdd_npu_s0>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknn_mmu_0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknn_core_1 {
+	npu-supply = <&vdd_npu_s0>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknn_mmu_1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &saradc {
 	vref-supply = <&vcca_1v8_s0>;
 	status = "okay";
-- 
Armbian

